 "notes": "Headline result: 95% C.L. COBE-FIRAS constraint on kinetic mixing epsilon (=chi) vs dark photon mass m_Ap from gamma->A prime resonant conversion CMB spectral distortions (Fig.4 = Fig.5 zoom). Traced the fiducial solid+dotted colored FIRAS line (free-streaming=purple, y-era=blue, mu-y transition=green, mu-era=orange, T-era=red) from vector PDF mAp_eps_plt_allbounds.pdf, lower-envelope of the excluded region. Y-axis calibrated from actual tick-mark vector positions (text baselines sit ~6px below ticks, which would bias the compressed full-range figure by ~1.6x; verified against the y-stretched zoomin Fig.5 giving plateau ~2.7e-8). Curve: free-streaming bathtub min ~2.2e-7 at ~5e-12 eV, bump ~2e-6 near 5e-11 eV, plateau eps~2.55-2.8e-8 over 1e-8..1e-4 eV, rising T-era wall at high mass. Not a dark-matter search (assumes negligible A prime abundance), so no density. Highest-mass points (>~5e-4 eV) are the green/red dotted portions where the paper flags the mu-y transition/large-distortion approximation as less robust; XENON1T supersedes there. epsilon reported directly (chi==epsilon).",
